  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\nThe ordering guarantee that applies to the integration built by this workspace — the revisioned state-change feed (`StateChangeFeed.changes`) that hosts/consumers (first deep consumer: Palimpsest) use to observe management-state commits — is **global**:\\n\\n> one ledger-wide, durable, monotonically increasing **commit-observation order** shared by all readers of the store. Record A's \\\"global\\\" statement is the operative ordering contract. Record B's \\\"per-consumer\\\" statement is operative only for **cursor ownership/storage**, not for the order relation.\\n\\n## What the guarantee actually is\\n\\n- **Single global position space.** `ordarium_state_changes(change_seq INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, …)` (`packages/ledger-sqlite/src/index.ts`, migrations v3→v4). `changePosition_i < changePosition_j` means \\\"i was committed and became observable before j\\\" — it does **not** claim causality, wall-clock time, or business priority.\\n- **Atomic with the commit.** The ordering row is inserted in the same SQLite transaction as the state CAS + refs, so `StateRevisionCommitted ⇔ observable` and `FailedStateCAS ⇒ NoFeedChange` (SCF‑INV‑1/2). The sequence is assigned by the storag",
